※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4605

※ `⎕isrecord` is a truth the compiler settles and not one a program works out, so it
※ stands in a condition `comptime` was written on and nowhere else -- which is the rule
※ `⎕typeof` follows and for the same reason: there is nothing for it to be at run time.
※
※ A program that wants the answer where a value goes has already been told it by the arm
※ it is standing in.

type Point = x: u8 ; y: u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let held: bool = ⎕isrecord(⌜Point⌝)
    if held: 0u6 else: 1u6
